�������������������������������������������\n\n������������������������������������"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|9|STARRED   |48", "t": "Import of Pulses", "head": "����������������������������������������\n��\n����������������������������������������\n��\n��������������������\n��\n��������������������������������������������������������\n��\n������������������������������������������������������������\n��������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��\n������������������������������������������������������\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n(a) whether any social and financial assistance policies for tribal and rural artists have been \ndevised by the Government; \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n(c) whether any steps have been taken by the Government to start and develop new art forms \nor cultures under Art Culture Development Scheme during the last two years; \n(d)  if so, the State-wise details thereof; \n(e) the details of the proposals submitted by various Cultural Organizations and the financial \nassistance provided to the said organizations and the achievements made under the said \nscheme during the last five years; and \n(f) the details of the financial assistance provided or the funds disbursed under the said \nscheme so far? \n \n \n��������������\n��\n��������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������������������������������������\n(a) Yes sir, the Ministry of Culture administers various schemes for providing financial \nassistance to the artists engaged in performing arts throughout the country including the \ntribal and rural artists.��\n(b) The names and details of the schemes mentioned at (a) above are placed at ���������������������� \n(c) No scheme by the name of Art Culture Development Scheme is administered by the \nMinistry of Culture. However, Ministry of Culture administers an Umbrella Scheme by the \nname of Kala Sanskriti Vikas Yojana (KSVY) under which all major arts forms & cultures of \nclassical, folk & tribal including vanishing arts are covered. \n(d) Does not arise in view of (c) above. \n(e) The details of the proposals of cultural organizations and financial assistance provided to \nthem during the last five years under the various schemes/scheme components of Kala \nSanskriti Vikas Yojana (KSVY) are placed at �������������������������� \n(f) The details of funds disbursed under Kala Sanskriti Vikas Yojana (KSVY) during five years \nare placed at ������������������������. \n\n��\n������������������������\n��\nAnnexure referred to in reply to part (b) of Lok Sabha Unstarred Question No. †48 for 18.07.2022 \n��\n������ �������������������� ���������������������� �������� �������������������� ������ �������������������������� ��������������������\n������������������������������������\n��\n The objective of this scheme is to provide financial support for all genres of performing arts \nactivities like dramatic groups, theatre groups, music ensembles, children theatre etc. and \nimparting training of artists by their respective Guru on regular basis in line with Guru–Shishya \nParampara. As per the scheme, support is provided to 1 Guru and maximum 18 Shishyas in the \nfield of theatre and 1 Guru and maximum 10 Shishyas in the field of music & dance. \n \nAmount of Assistance – Guru Rs.15000/- p.m., Shishya – Rs.2000-10000/-p.m (depending upon \nthe age of artist). \n�� ��\n��\n������ �������������� ������ �������������������� ���������������������� �������� �������������������� ������ �������� �������� ����������������������\nThe scheme consists of eight components. The names and details of the scheme \ncomponents are as given below: \n \n�������� ��������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��\n The objective of this scheme component is to provide support for cultural activities at Large \nscale National / International level. The Quantum of assistance under this scheme is up to Rs. 5 \nCr. \n \n���������� ����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��\n The objective of this scheme component is to provide financial support to NGOs/ Societies/ \nTrusts/ Universities etc. for Seminars, Conference, Research, Workshops, Festivals, Exhibitions, \nSymposia, Production of Dance, Drama-Theatre, Music etc.  The maximum grants provided under \nCFPG is Rs.5 Lakh (Rs. 20 Lakh under exceptional circumstances) \n \n������������ ������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��������������������\n��\n The objective of this scheme component is to promote and preserve the cultural heritage of \nthe Himalayas through research, training and dissemination through audio visual programmes. \nThe financial support is provided to the organizations in the States falling under the Himalayan \nRegion i.e. Jammu & Kashmir, Himachal Pradesh, Uttarakhand, Sikkim and Aruna"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|9|STARRED   |49", "t": "Transportation of Coal", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 49 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2022 \n \nTRANSPORTATION OF COAL \n \n* 49.  SHRI BRIJBHUSHAN SHARAN SINGH: \n SHRI P.P. CHAUDHARY: \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the current status of rakes deployed for transportation of coal to \npower plants across the country; \n \n(b) whether the Government has taken measures to deploy additional \nrakes to augment transportation of coal to power plants in the \nlight of recent developments and if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c) whether the Government plans to or has undertaken measures to \nupgrade coal rake wagons to incorporate upsurge in demand; \n \n(d) whether the Government has envisaged a role for ‘Startups for \nRailways’ policy to constructively resolve the issue and if so, the \ndetails thereof; and  \n \n(e) the details regarding distribution of coal for this financial year to \nthe States? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COMMUNICATIONS AND  \nELECTRONICS & INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \n \n(SHRI ASHWINI VAISHNAW) \n \n(a) to (e) : A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n***** \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (e) OF STARRED \nQUESTION NO. 49 BY SHRI BRIJBHUSHAN SHARAN SINGH  AND SHRI \nP.P. CHAUDHARY ANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 20.07.2022 REGARDING \nTRANSPORTATION OF COAL \n \n(a) & (b) : Considering the importance of coal transportation, Indian \nRailways has increased the deployment of rakes for coal loading to \npower houses.  D uring, first quarter of current financial year (April -June \n2022), Railways have deployed average 504 rakes per day for \ntransportation of coal to power plants across the country. Against this, \nthe coal loading to power sector during the period has been 434 rakes \nper day which is 32% more than the corresponding period of 2021 -22. In \nJuly 2022 (upto 13 th), Railways have deployed 504 rakes for \ntransportation of coal to power plants against which coal loading to \npower sector has been 425 rakes per day which is 41% more than the \ncorresponding period in July 2021.   \n \n(c): Besides augmenting additional rakes, Indian Railways has \nundertaken measures to deploy higher capacity wagons (BOXNS type) for \ncoal loading on routes which are fit for higher axle load operations and \nwhich have additional pay load of 13% over normal open wagons to meet \nthe enhanced demand.  \n \n(d): No, Sir. \n \n(e): In 2022 -23, Coal India Limited(CIL) has Annual Contracted Quantity \n(ACQ) under Fuel Supply Agreement (FSA) with State Power Gencos for a \nquantity   of  188.7  Million  Tonnes(MT).   Apart  from  this,  coal  is  being  \n \nContd….2/- \n\n: 2 : \nallocated to State Nominated Agencies of the concerned State(s) for \ncurrent Financial Year ( FY), to be supplied through FSA. Singareni \nCollieries Company Limited (SCCL) has plans to dispatch 70 MT during \nthe year 2022-23, out of which 57.8 MT is for power sector. \nThe State wise details of distribution of coals are as under: \n(in Million Tonnes) \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n***** \nState(s) FSA Quantity \nof the \nConcerned \nState \nGencos \nAllocation of \nCoal to State \nNominated \nAgencies of \nthe Concerned \nState(s) \nSCCL \nto \nPower \nsector \nCIL \nAndhra Pradesh 20.11 - 6.192 \nBihar - 0.14 - \nChhattisgarh 9.61 0.06 0.2 \nGujarat 14.02 0.09 - \nJharkhand 2 0.22 - \nJ&K - 0.01 - \nHaryana 10.88 0.01 - \nKarnataka 5.12 - 12.36 \nMadhya Pradesh 23.22 0.04 - \nMaharashtra 34.06 0.49 4.465 \nNagaland - 0.01 - \nOdisha 2.7 0.04 - \nPunjab 4.12 0.02 - \nRajasthan 16.71 0.02 - \nTamil Nadu 19.04 - 2.8 \nTripura - 0.02 - \nUttar Pradesh 23.8 0.28 - \nWest Bengal 3.32 0.1 1.0 \nTelangana - - 30.79 "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|9|STARRED   |5", "t": "Depreciation of Indian Currency", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF CULTURE \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.5 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 18.07.2022 \n \nMONUMENTS OF NATIONAL IMPORTANCE IN JHARKHAND. \n \n5. DR. NISHIKANT DUBEY: \nWill the Minister of Culture be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the number of monuments or sites declared as monument s of national \nimportance by the Archaeological Survey of India (ASI), State- wise including \nJharkhand; \n(b) the details of the funds spent on the said monuments or sites during the last five \nyears; \n(c) the revenue ear ned by the Government from these monuments during each of \nthe last three years; \n(d) whether the Government proposes to declare any other monument as monument \nof national importance; and \n(e) if so, the details thereof, State-wise? \n \