nt of expenditure incurred thereon; and \n(d) the total amount of subsidies and incentives provided to the entrepreneurs related to this sector, \nfarmers and common people for using solar energy,  State-wise? \n  \n ANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF NEW & RENEWABLE ENERGY AND POWER  \n(SHRI R.K. SINGH) \n(a) to (d) A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n***** \n \n \n  \n\nSTATEMENT  \n \nSTATEMENT REFFERED TO IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. \n165 FOR 28.07.2022 REGARDING GENERATION OF POWER THROUGH SOLAR \nENERGY \n \n(a) Central Electricity Authority has reported that the power generated through solar energy in \nthe country during the  last five years has been  as under: \nYear Electricity from Solar energy (in \nMU) \n2017-18 25871.07 \n2018-19 39268.19 \n2019-20 50131.09 \n2020-21 60402.26 \n2021-22 73483.94 \n \n(b) As on 30.6.2022, solar power projects of 57.71 GW have been installed in the country, 48.7 \nGW are under installation and 16.7  GW are under bidding ,   totaling 123.1  GW.   Total   installed \nsolar  capacity in Gujarat is 7.81 GW and 6.1GW is under installation. \n(c) Most of the solar power projects are installed by private sector d evelopers and as per the \nnormative cost of Rs. 4.5 Crore per MW, an expenditure of approximately Rs. 2.60 lakh crore has \nbeen incurred on solar installations of capacity 57.71 GW. \n(d) State-wise details of funds released under various solar schemes of Ministry of New and \nRenewable Energy (MNRE) during the last three years are given at Annexure. \n***** \n  \n\nANNEXURE REFFERED TO IN REPLY TO PART (d) OF LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO. 165 FOR 28.07.2022  \n \nSTATE-WISE DETAILS OF FUNDS RELEASED UNDER VARIOUS SOLAR \nSCHEMES OF MNRE DURING LAST THREE YEARS \n (Rs. in Crore) \n \nS.No. State 2019-20 2020-21 2021-22 \n1 Andhra Pradesh 194.04 51.49 10.48 \n2 Arunachal Pradesh 17.01 19.76 10.54 \n3 Andaman & Nicobar 6.77 0.35 37.97 \n4 Assam 33.07 0.00 9.19 \n5 Bihar  1.38 2.93 0.00 \n6 Cha