�������� ���� �������� ��� ���� ������\n������������ � ������� ���������� ���� ������������ ������ ������� �������� ���\n��������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��������������������� ��\n������� �\n�"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|9|UNSTARRED |300", "t": "Enrolment of Youth Volunteers", "head": " \n \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF AYURVEDA, YOGA & NATUROPATHY, UNANI, \nSIDDHA AND HOMOEOPATHY (AYUSH) \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.300 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 5TH AUGUST, 2022 \n \nSETTING UP OF CENTRAL RESEARCH INSTITUTIONS \n \n*300. SHRI PATEL HASMUKHBHAI SOMABHAI:  \n \nWill the Minister of AYUSH be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the Government has established Central Research Institutions (CRIs) in each \nState/UT;  \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof, State/UT-wise;  \n \n(c) the details of the funds provided by the Government for establishment of CRI in such \nStates/ UTs along with its utilization thereof; and  \n \n(d) the other steps taken/proposed to be taken by the Government to promote Private \nResearch Institutes? \n \n \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF AYURVEDA, YOGA & NATUROPATHY, UNANI,  \nSIDDHA AND HOMOEOPATHY(AYUSH) \n \n  \n(SHRI SARBANANDA SONOWAL) \n(a) to (d) A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.300* FOR 5TH AUGUST, 2022 \n \n(a) & (b) The Ministry of Ayush has established Central Research Institutes, functioning \nunder the purview of all five Research Councils – Central Council for Research in \nAyurvedic Sciences ( CCRAS); Central Council for Research in Sidha (CCRS); Central \nCouncil for Research in Unani Medicine ( CCRUM); Central Council of Research in \nHomeopathy ( CCRH); and Central Council of Research in Yoga &Naturopathy \n(CCRYN). In addition to the Central Research Institutes, each Research Council also  has \nRegional Research Institutes and Clinical Research Institutes/Units under its purview. The \ndetails of all Central Research Institutes, Regional Research Institutes, Clinical Research \nInstitutes/Units under each of the above mentioned Research Councils  are given in \nAnnexure. \n(c)    Details of funds provided by the Government for setting up of Central Research \nInstitutes, Council wise, are as under: \nCCRS: The amount of Rs . 58.57 Crores has been provided by the Government since \n2017-18, and the full amount has been utilised.     \nCCRUM: Earlier, CRIUM Lucknow being housed in rented accommodation was later \nshifted to its own building in 2014 an amount of Rs. 18.72 Crorewas incurred. Thus the \nwhole amount provided by the Government was fully utilised.  \nCCRH : Total funds provided by the Government for setting up of  its four CRIs has \nbeen to the tune of Rs.107.54 crores, whereas  the funds utilised so far utilized have \nbeen to the tune of Rs.72.90 crores, and remaining funds are under process of \nutilization. \nCCRYN: Total funds provided by the Government for its three  CRIs is Rs.121.24 \ncrores, and the full amount has been utilised. \nCCRAS: Total funds provided by the Government fo r its nine CRIs is Rs.70.9082 \ncrores, and the funds utilised so far have been to the tune of Rs.27.4252 crores. \n \n(d)      Several schemes of the Ministry of Ayush, like Extra Mural Research projects \n(EMR) (Ayush Oushadhi Gunvatta Evum Uttapadan Sanvardhan Yojna (AOGUSY \nScheme), Champion Services Sector Scheme , AYURSWASTHYA YOJANA, are \nunder implementation to  promote Private Research Institutes.  International/National \nConferences, Seminars, Workshops, Training Programmes are also organized to adopt the \nlatest medical advancements in research methodologies. \n \n******** \n\n \nAnnexure \n \n1. CENTRAL COUNCIL FOR RESEARCH IN AYURVEDIC SCIENCES (CCRAS) \nCentral Research Institutes: \ni. Central Ayurveda Research Institute, New Delhi \nii. Central Ayurveda Research Institute, Patiala, Punjab \niii. Central Ayurveda Research Institute, Bhubaneswar, Odisha \niv. Central Ayurveda Research Institute, Kolkatta, West Bengal \nv. Central Ayurveda Research Institute, Mumbai, Maharashtra \nvi. Central Ayurveda Research Institute, Jhansi, Uttar Pradesh \nvii. Central Ayurveda Research Institute, Bengaluru, Karnataka \nviii. Central Ayurveda Research Institute, Chennai, Tamil Nadu \nix. Central Ayurveda Research Institute, Guwahati, Assam \nRegional Research Institutes \ni. Regional Ayurveda Research Institute, Gwalior, Madhya Pradesh \nii. Regional Ayurveda Research Institute, Lucknow, Uttar Pradesh \niii. Regional Ayurveda Research Institute, Jaipur, Rajasthan \niv. Regional Ayurveda Research Institute, Nagpur, Maharashtra  \nv. Regional Ayurveda Research Institute, Thiruvananthapuram, Kerala \nvi. Regional Ayurveda Research Institute, Vijayawada, Andhra Pradesh \nvii. Regional Ayurveda Research Institute, Patna, Bihar \nviii. Regional Ayurveda Research Institute, Gangtok, Sikkim \nix. Regional Ayurveda Research Institute, Itanagar, Arunachal Pradesh \nx. Regional Ayurveda Research Institute, Jammu, Union Territory of Jammu & Kashmir \nxi. Regional Ayurveda Research Institute, Mandi, Himachal Pradesh \nxii. Regional Ayurveda Research Institute, Almora, Uttarakhand \nxiii. Regional Ayurveda Research Institute, Ahmedabad, Gujarat \nxiv. Regional Ayurveda Research Institute, Hyderabad, Telangana \nxv. Regional Ayurveda Research Institute,"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|9|UNSTARRED |301", "t": "Rise in Terror Attacks", "head": "�\n������������������� �\n������������ ������������ �\n�\n��������� �\n�� ������������������� ����� �\n�\n���������������������� �� �� ����� ��������������� ��� ������������� �\n�\n���������������������� �\n�\n����� �������������������������� �\n�\n������������������������������������������������������� �\n�\n��������������������������������������������������������� �������������\n�\n������������������������������������������������� ���������������������������\n���