|UNSTARRED |312", "t": "Setting up of Mega Food Park", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF FOOD PROCESSING INDUSTRIES \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 312 \nANSWERED ON 19TH JULY, 2022 \n  \nSETTING UP OF MEGA FOOD PARK \n  \n312. SHRI VISHNU DATT SHARMA: \n  \n             Will the Minister of FOOD PROCESSING INDUSTRIES be pleased to state: \n \n  \n(a) whether the Government has any proposal to set up Mega Food Park in Khajuraho \nParliamentary Constituency so as to build up cereal, millet and fruit based food \nprocessing economy in this relatively underdeveloped regions; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(c)  if not, the reasons therefor?  \n  \n \nANSWER \n \n  \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR FOOD PROCESSING INDUSTRIES \n(SHRI PRAHLAD SINGH PATEL) \n  \n(a) to (c): Ministry of Food Processing Industries (MoFPI) has been implementing various sub-\nschemes of the Pradhan Mantri Kisan Sampada Yojana (PMKSY), including the Mega Food \nPark (MFP) Scheme with the aim to create modern infrastructure for the food processing sector \nalong the value chain from farm to market. However, MoFPI does not set up MFPs on its own. \nThe scheme is demand driven and proposals are invited through Expression of Interest from \ntime to time and MoFPI extends financial support to the \"promoters\" of the approved projects \nas grants-in-aid. MoFPI has sanctioned 41 MFPs in 25 different States/UTs so far.  \n  \nAs regards Khajuraho Parliamentary Constituency, no MFP project has been \nsanctioned. However, two (02) MFP projects have been approved in Khargaon and Dewas \nDistrict of Madhya Pradesh.    \n  \nThe c ontinuation of the MFP Scheme from 1st April 2021 onward has not been \napproved by the Government.  \n \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|9|UNSTARRED |313", "t": "Incorporation of Scientific Methods in Fishing", "head": "�\n�\n������������������� �\n�������������������� �������������������� ������������ �\n�������������������� ����\n�\n��� ������ �\n�\n�