 - - - - \n18 Nagarkurnool 5  1,719  1,691  991  409  582  \n19 Narayanapet 2  499  499  107  99  8 \n20 Nalgonda 6  4,378  4,206  4,206  2,526  1,680  \n21 Nirmal 9  3,474  2,868  1,860  200  1,660  \n22 Nizamabad 9  4,622  4,531  2,757  1,341  1,416  \n23 Peddapalli 6  1,551  1,543  935  123  812  \n24 RajannaSircilla 5  2,941  2,923  2,151  263  1,888  \n25 RangaReddy 3  4,512  4,353  4,121  2,333  1,788  \n26 Sangareddy 8  4,261  4,122  4,122  2,045  2,077  \n27 Siddipet 16  6,366  6,056  5,749  919  4,830  \n28 Suryapet 8  3,683  3,551  3,551  1,935  1,616  \n29 Vikarabad 7  1,807  1,803  384  60  324  \n30 Wanaparthy 5  1,579  1,264  802  298  504  \n31 Warangal(Rural) 2  506  505  5 5 - \n32 Warangal(Urban) 13  7,278  7,025  6,249  3,716  2,533  \n33 YadadriBhuvanagiri 3  733  723  647  163  484  \n GrandTotal  303  2,47,079  2,35,044  2,09,576  81,248  1,28,328 "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|9|UNSTARRED |85", "t": "Promotion of SDS", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF TOURISM \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 85 \nANSWERED ON 18.07.2022 \n \nPROMOTION OF SDS \n \n85.   SHRIMATI MANJULATA MANDAL:  \n        SHRI GAJANAN KIRTIKAR:  \n        SHRI C.N. ANNADURAI:  \n        DR. PON GAUTHAM SIGAMANI:  \n        SHRI DHANUSH M. KUMAR:  \n        SHRI SELVAM G.:  \n \nWill the Minister of TOURISM be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the Government is progressing with Swadesh Darshan \nScheme (SDS) for boosting tourism sector and if so, the details \nthereof;  \n(b)  whether the Government has collaborated/proposes to collaborate \nwith some Non-Governmental players to promote SDS and if so, the \ndetails thereof and the steps taken by the Government in this \nregard;  \n(c)  the manner and extent to which such collaboration will help t o \nimprove tourism in the country;  \n(d)  whether the Government has taken steps for the development of \ntribal and rural circuits under SDS and if so, the details thereof;  \n(e)  whether the Union Government has received proposals from various \nStates includin g Odisha, Maharashtra and Tamil Nadu for the \ndevelopment of Tourism Circuits and if so, the details thereof and \nthe response of the Union Government thereto; and  \n(f)  whether all identified Tourism circuits have been made operational \nand if so, the detail s thereof including the number of tourists who \nparticipated in each circuit under the said scheme? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF TOURISM         (SHRI G. KISHAN REDDY) \n \n(a) to (f): Yes, Sir. The Ministry of Tourism has revamped its Swadesh \nDarshan scheme as Swad esh Darshan 2.0 (SD2.0) with the  \n\nobjective to develop sustainable and responsible destinations following \na tourist & destination centric approach. The guidelines for SD2.0 \nenvisage encouraging the States for opportunities for Private -Sector and \nPublic-Private Partnerships.  \n \nThe Ministry of Tourism under its  Central Sector Scheme - \nSwadesh Darshan  1.0 (SD1.0) has sanctioned 76 projects throughout the \ncountry including the S tates of Odisha, Maharashtra and Tamil  Nadu \nunder various thematic circuits.  The details of the projects sanctioned  \nunder Tribal & Rural circuit in   SD1.0 is as under: - \nTRIBAL CIRCUIT                    (Amt. in crore)     \nS. \nNo. \nState/UT Year of \nsanction \nName of the Project/ Year of \nSanction \nAmt. \nSanctioned \n1. Nagaland  (2015-16) Development of Tribal Circuit \nPeren- Kohima- Wokha \n97.36 \n2. Chhattisgarh  (2015-16) Development of Jashpur - \nKunkuri- Mainpat- Kamleshpur \n- Maheshpur -Kurdar - \nSarodhadadar- Gangrel- \nKondagaon– \nNathiyanawagaon- Jagdalpur- \nChitrakoot- Tirthgarh \n96.10 \n3. Telangana  (2016-17)                                                                                       Development of Mulugu -\nLaknavaram- Medavaram- \nTadvai- Damaravi- Mallur- \nBogatha Waterfalls \n79.87 \n4. Nagaland \n \n (2016-17) Development of Mokokchung-\nTuensang-Mon \n98.14 \n \nRURAL CIRCUIT              (Amt. in crore) \nS.No. Name \nof State \nYear of \nsanction \nProject Name Amt. \nSanctioned \n1. Bihar  (2017-18) Development of Bhitiharwa - \nChandrahia- Turkaulia \n44.65 \n2. Kerala  (2018-19) Development of Malanad \nMalabar Cruise Tourism Project \n80.37 \n\n \nThe details of the projects  sanctioned under SD1.0 in the S tate of \nOdisha, Maharashtra and Tamil Nadu is as under: \n(Amt. in crore) \nState Circuit Sanction \nYear \nName of the Project Amount \nSanctioned \nOdisha Coastal \nCircuit \n2016-17 Development of \nGopalpur, Barkul, \nSatpada and Tampara \n70.82 \nMaharashtra Coastal \nCircuit \n2015-16 Development of \nSindhudurg Coastal \nCircuit – Sagareshwar, \nTarkarli, Vijaydurg \n(Beach & Creek), \nMithbhav \n19.06 \nMaharashtra Spiritual \nCircuit \n2018-19 Development of Waki – \nAdasa – Dhapewada-\nParadsingha-\nTelankhandi-Girad \n47.53 \nTamil Nadu Coastal \nCircuit \n2016-17 Development of \nChennai-\nMammallapuram-\nRameshwaram – \nManpadu – \nKanyakumari \n73.13 \n \nOperation & Maintenance (O&M) of the assets created under \nSwadesh Darshan sc heme is undertaken by  the concerned State  \nGovernments/Union Territory Administrations.  The Ministry of Tourism is \nnot maintaining any data of the  number of tourists who participated  in \neach circuit under the scheme. \n******** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|9|UNSTARRED |850", "t": "National Merit cum means Scholarship", "head": " GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF MINORITY AFFAIRS \n  \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 850 \nANSWERED ON 21.07.2022 \n  \nNATIONAL MERIT CUM MEANS SCHOLARSHIP \n  \n850. SHRI MOHAMMED FAIZAL P.P.: \n        SHRI BENNY BEHANAN: \n  \nWill the Minister of MINORITY AFFAIRS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) the reasons for lower allocation for the National Merit-cum-Means Scholarship during \nthe financial year 2021-2022 budget as compared to financial year 2020-2021 as this has \nnegative effects on the education of disadvantaged youths; and \n \n(b) the details of the measures put in place to ensure the smooth and timely functioning of \nthe National Merit-cum-Means Scholarship and other schemes as students have reported \nbureaucratic hurdles that prevent full uptake? \n             \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF MINORITY AFFAIRS  \n(SHRIMATI SMRITI ZUBIN IRANI) \n  \n(a):      Ministry of Minority Affairs implements a number of Educational Empowerment \nSchemes, namely Pre-Matric Scholarship Scheme, Post-Matric Scholarship Scheme, \nMerit-cum-Mean based Scholarship Scheme (MCM), Begum Hazrat Mahal National \nScholarship (BHMNS), Maulana Azad National Fellowship Scheme (MANF), Padho \nPardesh, Naya Savera and Nai Udaan for Educational Empowerment of students \nbelonging to the economically weaker sections of the six notified minority communities \ni.e. Buddhist, Christian, Jain, Muslim, Sikh and Zoroastrian (Parsi) in all States across the \ncountry.  \n  \nThe Budget Estimate (BE) for a Fiscal Year is firmed up on the basis of expenditure \nmade under a Scheme up to the 3rd quarter of the previous fiscal whereas in the year \n\n2020-21 more than 70% of the expenditure under the Merit-cum-Means based \nScholarship Scheme (MCM) Scheme was booked in the last  quarter.  Nonetheless, \nhigher numbers of Scholarships (1,31,810) were sanctioned under MCM in 2021-22 \ncompared to 2020-21 (1,20,371).   \n \n(b): All the 3 Scholarship Schemes of this Ministry, including MCM, are implemented \nthrough the online Portal i.e.  National Scholarship Portal (NSP) along with other \nScholarship Schemes of the Government and the Scholarships are disbursed directly in \nthe bank accounts of beneficiaries under Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT) mode ensuring \ntransparency in the implementation process. Further, in order to enable maximum number \nof students to apply the Portal was kept open in 2021-22 for almost 5 months from \n18.08.2021 to 15.01.2022. In 2021-22 the process for payment of   renewal scholarships \nwas also started early in November, 2022.  \n  \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|9|UNSTARRED |851", "t": "Inter-State Coordination for Dam Water Storage", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA  \nMINISTRY OF JAL SHAKTI, \nDEPARTMENT OF WATER RESOURCES, RIVER DEVELOPMENT & GANGA \nREJUVENATION \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 851 \nANSWERED ON 21.07.2022 \n \nINTER-STATE COORDINATION FOR DAM WATER STORAGE \n851 SHRI SHRINIWAS PATIL \nWill the Minister of JAL SHAKTI be pleased to state: - \n(a) whether the Government has envisaged or already  put in place any mechanism for inter-State \ncoordination of dam water storage and water release  to avoid upstream flooding in the Krishna \nriver basin in western Maharashtra which leads to s evere floods in Satara, Sangli and Kolhapur \ndistricts of Maharashtra especially in the monsoon season; and \n(b) if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER  \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR JAL SHAKTI  \n(SHRI BISHWESWAR TUDU ) \n \n(a) & (b)  For effective inter-state coordination of dam wate r storage and water release to avoid \nupstream flooding in the Krishna river basin in wes tern Maharashtra, regular meetings of all \nstakeholders are held. Recently, a meeting on 'Prep aredness for Flood Management for Krishna \nBasin' was held at Hyderabad with the project authorities of important reservoirs in Krishna Basin, \nofficials of Water Resources Department, Disaster M anagement Department of the states of \nMaharashtra, Karnataka, Telangana and Andhra Prades h, Indian Metrological Deportment (IMD) \nHyderabad, National Remote Sensing Centre (NRSC) an d Central Water Commission in May, \n2022 under the Chairmanship of Chief Engineer, Kris hna & Godavari Basin Organisation, CWC. \nThe modalities for data exchange and monitoring of flood between Karnataka and Maharashtra \nwere discussed. Further, Inter State Flood Coordina tion Committee (IFCC) has been established \nbetween Maharashtra and Karnataka for proper manage ment of floods in Krishna Basin. Besides \nabove, an Inter-state coordination meeting has take n place under the chairmanship of Chief \nSecretary, Government of Maharashtra with all stake holders regarding preparedness for flood in \nmonsoon season. \n \n***** \n \n \n\n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|9|UNSTARRED |852", "t": "Road Projects in Odisha", "head": "  \n GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION  No. 852 \nANSWERED ON 21st JULY, 2022 \n  \nROAD PROJECTS IN ODISHA \n  \n852.    SHRI BASANTA KUMAR PANDA: \n  \n       Will the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n  \nसड़क परिवहन औि िाजमार्गमंत्री \nbe pleased to state: \n  \n(a) the details and the present status of all ongoing road/ National \nHighway Projects in the State of Odisha;  \n(b) whether new road projects are being proposed for the State and if \nso, the details thereof; and  \n(c) the expenditure incurred on the said projects in the State during \nthe last three years and the current year? \n  \nANSWER \n  \nTHE MINISTER OF ROAD TRANSPORT & HIGHWAYS \n  \n(Shri NITIN JAIRAM GADKARI) \n  \n(a)      The details & the present status of ongoing National Highway \nprojects in the state of Odisha are at Annexure-I. \n  \n(b)     The details of National Highway projects sanctioned but yet to be \nawarded/awarded but appointed date yet to be given in the State of \nOdisha are at Annexure -II. The details of National Highway projects \nproposed for sanction in th e State of Odisha during 2022 -23 are at \nAnnexure-III.  \n\n(c)     The details of expenditure on NH developmental works during last \n3 years and current year in the State of Odisha are as below: \nYear 2019-20 2020-21 2021-22 2022-23 \nExpenditure  4651.00 4621.00 4618.00 904.00 \n  \n  \n\n  \nANNEXURE-I \n  \nANNEXURE-I REFERRED TO IN REPLY to PART (a) OF LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 852 FOR ANSWER FOR 21.07.2022 ASKED \nBY SHRI BASANTA KUMAR PANDA REGARDING ROAD PROJECTS IN \nODISHA. \n  \nDetails and the present status of ongoing 